From 906949ba8b5933f10f0d71fe4847174c4c6d56c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:08:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: advance MPEG geometry interval watermark

Do not keep the original sequence offset forever when geometry stays
unchanged. Advance the retained interval to each exact completed packet
so signed offset comparisons remain within the bounded FIFO distance.

The compiled production selector regression previously aborted after
2 GiB of same-size input. It now passes progress past 4 GiB, changes
across u32 wrap and future interval selection without changing pixels.

Change-Id: Ic232b7b9d09e7d54566dade1e057cb3f33e9985f
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
index 33ae0d3e1f01..80a565584569 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
@@ -935,6 +935,11 @@ static int mpeg12_multi_picture_format(struct mpeg12_multi *m,
 		kfree(f);
 		f = next;
 	}
+	/* Completion offsets advance in coded order within the bounded FIFO.
+	 * Move the retained interval's watermark so unchanged geometry remains
+	 * valid across 2 GiB and full 32-bit stream-offset wraparound.
+	 */
+	f->offset = pic->packet_offset;
 	pic->width = f->width;
 	pic->height = f->height;
 	return 0;
-- 
2.47.3

